), (\"8.41–ETO26097\",\"31D36D05\"), (\"8.43–ETO31478\",\"E35DF3C0\"), (\"8.50/1.5\",\"1C146AF7\"), (\"8.51–ETO22243\",\"B18A0CB3\")\n\nI'll add a \"remarks\" column for the no-checksum entries.\n\n5700 software rows (software_component, version, checksum, remarks):\nTransmitter Software (Weights & Measures):\n(\"1.20 (1.0)\",\"2DF0D8E9\"), (\"1.30 (1.1)\",\"ADE631BB\"), (\"1.85 (2.0) ETO28130\",\"0EA71B41\"), (\"2.00 (2.0)\",\"2F52132D\"), (\"2.10 (2.0)\",\"23DD3385\"), (\"3.0 (3.0)\",\"06108400\"), (\"3.1 (3.0)\",\"2DE64BB2\"), (\"3.2 (3.0)\",\"8CB1FE4B\"), (\"4.0 (3.0)\",\"0E4997D5\"), (\"4.07 (4.0)\",\"44477758\"), (\"4.1 (4.0)\",\"AFE0673B\"), (\"4.2 (4.0)\",\"627B3E99\"), (\"4.30 (4.0)\",\"AC509A54\")\nremarks: \"Version (x.x) = W&M software version; W&M software has no checksum\" — maybe put once in footnotes.\n\nInternal Core Processor: 17 rows as listed.\nPIC Firmware: (\"8.0\",\"0000DE9C\")\nLCD PIC Firmware: (\"3.0\",\"000081D5\",\"for transmitter software 1.20\"), (\"3.0\",\"00007442\",\"for transmitter software 1.30 and later\")\n\nOK. Also include footnotes for *) and **) of both tables.\n\nThe overall JSON will be long but fine.\n\nNow double-check numbers with commas: \"1,8\" → 1.8 ✓; \"0,033\" → 0.033 ✓; \"0,067\" → 0.067 ✓; \"0,46\" → 0.46 ✓; \"2,72\" → 2.72 ✓; \"0,017\" → 0.017 ✓; \"0,23\" → 0.23 ✓; \"1,36\" → 1.36 ✓; \"0,05\" → 0.05 ✓; \"0,5\" → 0.5 ✓.\n\nDensity: 400 … 1100 kg/m³ → {min:400,max:1100} kg/m³.\n\nNow certificate-level \"characteristics\" type_level — final list:\n- accuracy_class: {\"value\": \"0.3; 0.5; 1.0; 1.5\", \"unit_symbol\": null} — hmm or in recommendation only. Include both; fine.\n- density_range: kg/m³\n- maximum_viscosity: mm²/s\n- environmental_classes (measurement sensor): string\n- ambient_temperature_range (measurement sensor): °C\n- measured_liquids: string\n\nSince these pertain to the sensor, I'll add them to the sensor component AND keep type_level minimal? Duplication vs placement... The schema says type_level is whole-cert attributes. I'll place them at type_level (they describe the certified transducer's essential characteristics) and also not duplicate in the component. Actually I earlier put them in sensor component. Decide: put general Table 1 chars in type_level, electronics chars in components, flow model chars in model_level, conditional in config_level, tables in matrix_tables. Components then hold documentation_folder + power supply etc. for electronics, and documentation folder for sensor. That avoids duplication. Sensor component characteristics: documentation_folder only. Good.\n\nAlso description of certified_type: \"Measurement transducer consisting of a CMF series or CMFHC series measurement sensor combined with MVD series or 5700 electronics. Documentation folders: TC7056-13 (measurement sensor), TC7057-16 (MVD series electronics), TC8519-4 (5700 electronics).\"\n\nNow footnotes array:\n[\n {\"marker\":\"[1]\",\"text\":\"With xxx or x denoting the size of the measurement sensor.\"},\n {\"marker\":\"y\",\"text\":\"y is a letter which indicates the type of material the meter is built of. Where there are different possibilities for a characteristic, the actual letter is indicated in superscript.\"},\n {\"marker\":\"(i)\",\"text\":\"CMF400: serial number up to 411000.\"},\n {\"marker\":\"(ii)\",\"text\":\"CMF400: serial number from 411000 up to 14200000.\"},\n {\"marker\":\"(iii)\",\"text\":\"CMF400: serial number higher than 14200000.\"},\n {\"marker\":\"*)\",\"text\":\"Software versions for the 1700 / 2700 which do not have a checksum (MVD series electronics, Table 5).\"},\n {\"marker\":\"**)\",\"text\":\"Software versions for the 2500 which do not have a checksum (MVD series electronics, Table 5).\"},\n {\"marker\":\"*)\",\"text\":\"The transmitter software and the Weights & Measures (W&M) software form a matched set. Please note that the W&M software does not have a checksum and means W&M is licensed (5700 electronics, Table 7).\"},\n {\"marker\":\"**)\",\"text\":\"The number between brackets, is the transmitter software which belongs to the stated checksum (5700 electronics, Table 7).\"}\n]\n\nTest reports roles: I'll mark the two NMi-3073006-xx and NMi-2591028-01 as... they're recent revision reports. Keep \"test_report\" for all. Actually maybe \"evaluation_report\"? The enum includes evaluation_report. NMi reports supporting OIML CS are typically \"OIML Type Evaluation Reports\". The cert: \"tests and examinations provided in the associated reports\". Without explicit labels, \"test_report\" is safe. Hmm, but the main type evaluation report for project 3073006... NMi-3073006-01/02 are likely the Type Evaluation Report for this certificate. I can't be certain of which; keep all test_report. Actually, let me mark all as \"test_report\" — consistent.\n\nDocumentation files: add to test_reports with role documentation_file:\n- {\"id\":\"TC7056-13\",\"role\":\"documentation_file\"} with date null pages null — omit missing fields per rule 8? I'll include \"date\": null, \"pages\": null? Rule: omit if not present. I'll omit keys.\n\nNow assemble everything. Also issuing_authority oiml_issuer_id \"NL1\"; certificate.oiml_issuer_id \"NL1\".\n\nPerson title: \"Certification Board\" — appears above the NMi Certin B.V. signature block; likely the signer's department. I'll set person_title: \"Certification Board\". Reasonable.\n\nLet me also double check page 4 table parse: header row: Sensor type | CMF200y | CMF300y | CMF350y | CMF400y. Rows:\n- Max flow: 1450, 4500, 4920, 6800 ✓\n- Min flow class 0.3: 36, 114, 453(A,B,C,E)/226(H,L,M,P), 680(i)/680(ii)/1700(iii) ✓\n- Min flow class \"0.5;\" row: rowspan 18 (CMF200), 57 (CMF300), 226(A,B,C,E)/113(H,L,M,P) (CMF350), and CMF400 cell: 680(i)/340(ii)/850(iii) ✓\n- Min flow class \"1.0; 1.5\" row: CMF400 cell 680(i)/340(ii)/340(iii) ✓\n- Min measured quantity: 20, 200, 500, 500 ✓\n- Max pressure: 25 ×4 ✓\n\nGood, matches my earlier reading.\n\nCheck CMF010y values: max 1.8 (from \"1,8\"); min class 0.3: 0.033(H,L,M)/0.067(P); min class 0.5/1.0/1.5: 0.017(H,L,M)/0.033(P); MMQ 0.05; max pressure 25. ✓\n\nCMF100y min class 0.3 = 11.4; ✓.\n\nCMFHC: max flow 12600, 22000, 30000 ✓. Min 0.3: 1136, 2268, 3400. 0.5: 568, 1134, 1700. 1.0: 284, 567, 850. 1.5: 227, 453, 680. MMQ 1000 each. Pressure 25. ✓\n\nNow write JSON. Be careful with the en-dash/– characters: \"3.0–ETO17153\" uses en dash; fine in JSON.\n\nUse \"kg/m³\" symbol; \"mm²/s\"; \"°C\".\n\nOne more consideration: recommendation.accuracy_classes: [\"0.3\",\"0.5\",\"1.0\",\"1.5\"].\n\nrecommendation: {\"id\": \"R117-1\", \"edition\": 2007, \"amendment\": null, \"scheme\": \"A\", \"accuracy_classes\": [\"0.3\",\"0.5\",\"1.0\",\"1.5\"]}. Amendment unknown — omit.\n\ncertificate.scheme \"A\".\n\nLet me now also think about \"page_total\": 8.\n\nWrite the final JSON. I'll be meticulous about commas/braces. Given length, structure carefully.\n\nAlso for model entries attributes: include per-model key attributes? I'll keep minimal attributes {\"series\": \"CMF\"} etc. Also include the y-letter note? label can carry: label \"CMF010y (CMF series, y = tube material letter)\". Good.\n\nFinal JSON structure:\n\n{\n  \"certificate\": {...},\n  \"issuing_authority\": {...},\n  \"applicants\": [...],\n  \"manufacturers\": [...],\n  \"certified_type\": {...},\n  \"model_family\": {...},\n  \"components\": [...],\n  \"characteristics\": {\"type_level\": {...}, \"model_level\": [...], \"config_level\": [...]},\n  \"matrix_tables\": [...],\n  \"recommendation\": {...},\n  \"test_reports\": [...],\n  \"revision_history\": [...],\n  \"footnotes\": [...]\n}\n\nType_level values with structured shape: include unit_symbol and unit_id and footnote_markers? Rule 2 says every characteristic value must be object with value/unit_symbol/unit_id/footnote_markers shape. I'll include unit_id: null and footnote_markers: [] where applicable. For string values, unit_symbol null.\n\nLet me write it all out now.\n\nFor model_level, values entries: {\"model\": \"...\", \"value\": N} plus unit at attribute level (schema example: {\"attribute\",\"unit_symbol\",\"values\"}). Values may include footnote_markers where needed — e.g., CMF350y/CMF400y not included there. CMF010y not included either. OK no footnote markers needed in model_level.\n\nWait — should CMF200y class 0.3 min flow = 36 have footnote? No markers. Fine.\n\nNow config_level for liquid temp ranges: entries:\n\n{\n  \"attribute\": \"liquid_temperature_range_mass_measurement\",\n  \"axis\": \"accuracy class\",\n  \"values\": [\n    {\"condition\": \"0.3 / 0.5 / 1.0\", \"value\": {\"min\": -10, \"max\": 250}, \"unit_symbol\": \"°C\"},\n    {\"condition\": \"1.5\", \"value\": {\"min\": -200, \"max\": 50}, \"unit_symbol\": \"°C\"}\n  ]\n},\n{\n  \"attribute\": \"liquid_temperature_range_density_and_volume_measurement\",\n  \"axis\": \"accuracy class\",\n  \"values\": [\n    {\"condition\": \"0.3 / 0.5 / 1.0\", \"value\": {\"min\": -10, \"max\": 150}, \"unit_symbol\": \"°C\"}\n  ]\n}\n\nAlso 5700 ambient config? I put in component. Fine.\n\nNow write everything. Also note Table 4 lists \"820\" in env classes — include MVD 820 in type list. Software tables don't show 820 software; fine.\n\nAlright, compose final answer. Careful: JSON valid — no comments, no trailing commas.\n\nAlso, the min flow config for CMF010y: the superscripts H, L, M / P: condition strings. And in matrix table rows I use strings \"0.033 (H, L, M); 0.067 (P)\".\n\nTime to write the output.",
